# Small Functions, Single Responsibility

## Hard limits

- **Max ~30 lines of logic per function** (excluding blank lines and trivial type-only noise). If longer, split.
- **One responsibility per function**: one reason to change. Extract helpers instead of nesting multi-step workflows.
- Prefer many small named functions over one large procedure or “god” component/hook.

## How to split

- Separate: validation → transformation → I/O → UI wiring.
- Extract domain logic out of React components and hooks into pure functions/services.
- Avoid deep nesting; early return and small helpers instead.

## Bad vs good

```ts
// ❌ BAD — monolithic handler
async function onConfirm() {
  // validate, map, call API, update store, navigate, toast — all inline, 80+ lines
}

// ✅ GOOD — composed steps
async function onConfirm() {
  const input = parseConfirmInput(raw);
  const result = await confirmQrLogin(input);
  applyConfirmSuccess(result);
}
```

Do not merge unrelated concerns to “save files.” Clarity and testability win.
